'''''Ypomonetikochelys''''' is an [[Extinction|extinct]] [[Monotypic taxon|monotypic genus]] of [[Proganochelyidae|proganochelyid]] [[turtle]] that inhabited [[Greenland]] during the [[Norian]] [[Stage (stratigraphy)|stage]] of the [[Late Triassic]] [[Geologic time scale|epoch]].

== Etymology ==
The [[Generic name (biology)|generic name]] ''Ypomonetikochelys'' derives from the [[Greek language|Greek]] words ''ypomonetikós'' and ''khélūs'', meaning patient and tortoise, respectively. The [[Binomial nomenclature|specific epithet]] of the [[type species]], ''Ypomonetikochelys euryaspis'', consists of the Greek words ''eurus'', meaning wide, and ''aspis'', meaning [[shield]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Szczygielski |first1=Tomasz |last2=Dróżdż |first2=Dawid |date=27 March 2026 |title=Triassic turtles ( Testudinata : Proterochersidae and Proganochelyidae ) of Greenland |url=https://academic.oup.com/zoolinnean/article/doi/10.1093/zoolinnean/zlag011/8544869 |journal=[[Zoological Journal of the Linnean Society]] |language=en |volume=206 |issue=3 |doi=10.1093/zoolinnean/zlag011 |issn=0024-4082 |access-date=3 April 2026 |via=Oxford Academic|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

